{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"77fa3da3","metadata":{"id":"77fa3da3"},"source":["# What Actually Drives a Good Patient Experience? HCAHPS Hospital Satisfaction Analysis\n","\n","**Author:** Toyin (Oloruntoba Oluwatoyin)\n","**Tools:** Python (pandas), SQL (SQLite), matplotlib, Google Colab\n","**Data:** CMS \"Patient Survey (HCAHPS) - Hospital\" — real, public, national patient-experience survey, pulled live via the CMS Provider Data API\n","\n","---\n","\n","## The business problem\n","\n","Imagine I'm a data analyst for a hospital network. The Chief Experience Officer asks:\n","\n","> **\"Patient experience scores affect how much Medicare pays us. Which specific parts of the patient's stay matter most for their overall opinion of us, and where should we focus first if we want to improve?\"**\n","\n","To answer this, I used HCAHPS: a national survey every Medicare-participating hospital in the US has to run, asking real discharged patients about their stay, things like whether nurses communicated well, whether the room was quiet at night, and whether they'd recommend the hospital.\n","\n","## What I will do in this notebook\n","\n","1. Pull the real data straight from CMS's own public API (no manual download needed)\n","2. Check it and clean it\n","3. Reshape it from \"one row per question\" into \"one row per hospital\" so I can compare measures side by side\n","4. Use SQL to find which specific measures matter most, how much hospitals vary by state, and whether small survey sizes bias the results\n","5. Chart the findings\n","6. Write a plain-language summary and be honest about the limits\n","\n","## The 9 things HCAHPS actually measures (star rating, 1 to 5)\n","\n","| Measure | What it's asking |\n","|---|---|\n","| Nurse communication | Did nurses communicate well? |\n","| Doctor communication | Did doctors communicate well? |\n","| Communication about medicines | Were new medicines explained clearly? |\n","| Discharge information | Did staff explain recovery care and symptoms to watch for? |\n","| Cleanliness | Was the room and bathroom kept clean? |\n","| Quietness | Was the area quiet at night? |\n","| Overall hospital rating | 0-10 rating, converted to a 1-5 star scale |\n","| Would recommend hospital | Would the patient recommend this hospital? |\n","| Summary star rating | CMS's single combined star score |"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"92f481c4","metadata":{"id":"92f481c4"},"source":["## Step 1: Pull the data straight from CMS's API\n","\n","I didn't download a file for this one. CMS has a public API that lets you query their data directly, so I connected to it straight from Colab.\n","Two things I ran into: CMS's API only gives back 500 rows per request, no matter what you ask for, and it only accepts one simple condition in the WHERE clause at a time (no lists, no wildcards). So the code below pulls each of the 9 measures separately, in batches of 500 each, and stacks all the results together. For roughly 43,000 rows, that's about 90 requests total, so this cell can take a couple of minutes to finish. That's expected, just let it run."]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import requests\n","import pandas as pd\n","import time\n","\n","BASE_URL = \"https://data.cms.gov/provider-data/api/1/datastore/sql\"\n","DISTRIBUTION_ID = \"b42ae2a7-5512-5cb4-b429-d3eaaab212d7\"\n","\n","dq = chr(34)  # a double-quote character\n","\n","measure_ids = [\"H_COMP_1_STAR_RATING\", \"H_COMP_2_STAR_RATING\", \"H_COMP_5_STAR_RATING\",\n","               \"H_COMP_6_STAR_RATING\", \"H_CLEAN_STAR_RATING\", \"H_QUIET_STAR_RATING\",\n","               \"H_HSP_RATING_STAR_RATING\", \"H_RECMND_STAR_RATING\", \"H_STAR_RATING\"]\n","\n","all_rows = []\n","\n","for measure in measure_ids:\n","    offset = 0\n","    while True:\n","        query = f\"[SELECT * FROM {DISTRIBUTION_ID}][WHERE hcahps_measure_id = {dq}{measure}{dq}][LIMIT 500 OFFSET {offset}]\"\n","        resp = requests.get(BASE_URL, params={\"query\": query, \"show_db_columns\": \"true\"})\n","\n","        if resp.status_code != 200:\n","            print(f\"Error on {measure} at offset {offset}:\", resp.status_code)\n","            print(resp.text[:300])\n","            break\n","\n","        batch = resp.json()\n","        if not batch:\n","            break\n","\n","        all_rows.extend(batch)\n","        offset += 500\n","\n","        if len(batch) < 500:\n","            break\n","\n","        time.sleep(0.3)\n","\n","    print(f\"{measure}: {offset if offset else len(batch)} rows pulled so far (running total: {len(all_rows)})\")\n","\n","df = pd.DataFrame(all_rows)\n","print(\"\\nDone. Total rows pulled:\", len(df))\n","print(\"Columns:\", df.columns.tolist())\n","df.head()"],"metadata":{"id":"MQO-A0uv5D57","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":724},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1790882411980,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":173273,"user":{"displayName":"Ayo","userId":"05827135324850076928"}},"outputId":"f100ff9e-7fb8-4972-a691-bdc4cdd66f36"},"id":"MQO-A0uv5D57","execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["H_COMP_1_STAR_RATING: 5000 rows pulled so far (running total: 4790)\n","H_COMP_2_STAR_RATING: 5000 rows pulled so far (running total: 9580)\n","H_COMP_5_STAR_RATING: 5000 rows pulled so far (running total: 14370)\n","H_COMP_6_STAR_RATING: 5000 rows pulled so far (running total: 19160)\n","H_CLEAN_STAR_RATING: 5000 rows pulled so far (running total: 23950)\n","H_QUIET_STAR_RATING: 5000 rows pulled so far (running total: 28740)\n","H_HSP_RATING_STAR_RATING: 5000 rows pulled so far (running total: 33530)\n","H_RECMND_STAR_RATING: 5000 rows pulled so far (running total: 38320)\n","H_STAR_RATING: 5000 rows pulled so far (running total: 43110)\n","\n","Done. Total rows pulled: 43110\n","Columns: ['record_number', 'facility_id', 'facility_name', 'address', 'citytown', 'state', 'zip_code', 'countyparish', 'telephone_number', 'hcahps_measure_id', 'hcahps_question', 'hcah